1
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:06,820
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:33,560
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,200
Dear Mom, Dad,

4
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:41,000
Big Big Brother, Middle Big Brother,

5
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:44,860
Little Big Brother, Dougie, Henri, Rodney,

6
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:48,100
Mikey, and Little Sandra, how are you?

7
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:49,580
I'm doing just fine.

8
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,780
Good morning, I'm sleepy.

9
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:59,057
Millie, you stayed up all night writing
home to your family again, didn't you?

10
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:00,897
That's what happens when
you write to each of them

11
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:03,857
separately down to the last
little niece and nephew.

12
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:04,770
Daddy!

13
00:02:04,853 --> 00:02:05,777
At least it pays off.

14
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:06,977
I'm getting rave reviews.

15
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:08,677
They call my letters the Millie Monthly.

16
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:11,377
Quality aside, you could have
written several books by now.

17
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:12,717
What's so weird about that?

18
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,035
Don't you write home?

19
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:18,697
Uh, yeah, well, I used to write at
first, but it's been a long time.

20
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:21,309
But I think for most
people, that's normal.

21
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:22,470
Besides,

22
00:02:22,553 --> 00:02:26,337
what would they say if I told them I
was hanging out with Vash the Stampede?

23
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:28,597
So you just don't want to write, Meryl?

24
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,268
It's not that I don't
want to write to them.

25
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:37,339
I guess it sounds pretty lame to
say that I just don't have the time.

26
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:52,269
Oh, gee, sorry about that.

27
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:54,937
I must have accidentally
pulled the trigger.

28
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:56,040
How dare you?

29
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:58,437
You have a lot of nerve,
you impudent scoundrel.

30
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:01,697
We're not dumb enough to be scared
by you and your rotten friends.

31
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:03,577
Oh, yes, it's become clear to me now.

32
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:06,297
There's a lot of meaning
behind those words, friends.

33
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:09,177
So stand up with your heads held
high and say what you want to say.

34
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:11,997
We won't give up our land
no matter what you do to us.

35
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:12,910
Yeah,

36
00:03:12,993 --> 00:03:15,417
we're not going to take this anymore, and
you can go back and tell that to Morgan.

37
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,337
Did you hear what I said, you old geezers?

38
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:18,420
Hey, come on now.

39
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:20,037
My gun went off by mistake.

40
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:25,160
You know that he mistake my
ass you fat lift golem. What?

41
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:28,580
What did you say a golem?

42
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:29,610
Ha

43
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,820
It's so hard my pistols twitching

44
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:45,280
You have no idea how dangerous that was.

45
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:48,140
If you make this broomhead mad,

46
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:51,897
I guarantee he'll leave you with a lot
more than injuries and property damage.

47
00:03:51,980 --> 00:03:52,840
Good God.

48
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:57,652
You're the ones who are dangerous,
clotheslining him from behind like that.

49
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:07,937
Meryl, that's a small
sacrifice for a great cause.

50
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:09,280
I know, that's right.

51
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,499
Way to go, Millie.

52
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,706
That's all you've got to say?

53
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:15,880
Did you say bodyguards?

54
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:17,290
Exactly.

55
00:04:17,373 --> 00:04:20,457
If you two were here to protect
us, we'd feel a whole lot safer.

56
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:21,957
I'm sorry, thanks anyway,

57
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:25,697
but company regulations strictly forbid
us from taking any part-time jobs.

58
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:26,610
I understand.

59
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:28,077
How about you, son?

60
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:28,990
Are you interested?

61
00:04:29,073 --> 00:04:30,297
Why the hell are you asking him?

62
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:34,957
The way that he moved when he pretended
us back there, he was exceptionally brave.

63
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:35,870
You don't say.

64
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:36,937
Well, it's nothing.

65
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:38,200
I do the best I can.

66
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:40,580
Absolutely no way.

67
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:43,180
How could you ask him?

68
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:44,897
Don't you know who this
broom head is, mister?

69
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:45,897
What is it, little lady?

70
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:46,810
You want the job?

71
00:04:46,893 --> 00:04:47,723
No.

72
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:49,540
Well, that's great.

73
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:51,237
Only you would think
of using your position

74
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:53,732
to help out people who are truly in need.

75
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:56,080
Well, we have no choice.

76
00:04:56,560 --> 00:05:00,854
I think the situation represents the
category of risk prevention to the T

77
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,697
Why have you decided to come with us mr.

78
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:06,610
Bash?

79
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:08,137
Well, I don't know.

80
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:09,577
I guess something was bothering me.

81
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:11,297
That's all keep out of this one.

82
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:12,437
Do you understand me?

83
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,350
Yes, ma 'am

84
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,980
You see that that's our land there

85
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,040
This is incredible!

86
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:38,855
How is all of this here if
there's no access to a ship?

87
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:39,850
Amazing!

88
00:05:39,933 --> 00:05:41,248
It's just like a geo-plant!

89
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:45,040
No, it's not just like it.

90
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,356
This is a geo-plant.

91
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:52,180
Yes, we believe that a geo-plant ran along
a mineral vein to form this offshoot.

92
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:57,282
The land value has skyrocketed so high It's
worth as much as a ship 300 yards wide.

93
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:01,617
That may be, but it couldn't have
gotten this far without a lot of help.

94
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:04,465
It would have taken a
massive amount of effort.

95
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:06,320
I remember it clearly.

96
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:10,860
Twenty years ago it was a tiny bud,
but I couldn't believe my eyes.

97
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:14,937
Just imagining how we could
raise such lush, beautiful land?

98
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:19,079
On an arid planet like this, you
have no idea how that kept us going.

99
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,430
That's right.

100
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:26,440
Our lives, our dreams, and
our hopes are all here.

101
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:29,457
It is amazing what you've done here,

102
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:32,017
but what does this have to do
with you hiring bodyguards?

103
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:34,257
You saw what happened back there in town.

104
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:36,000
That was not the first time.

105
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:37,377
The landowner, Morgan,

106
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:41,519
has been threatening us time and
again to hand over the deed or else.

107
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,555
But that is all going to end tomorrow.

108
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:49,061
Once we get this deed over to City
Hall, there's nothing he can do.

109
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:51,756
Hey, guys, it's time to change ships.

110
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:55,807
Oh, it's freezing out there.

111
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,294
It gets cold at night.

112
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:00,185
I appreciate all of your help.

113
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,755
Hey, it's no problem.

114
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:05,357
Since we were little kids, this place
has always been our playground, huh?

115
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:07,217
Yeah, and we're never gonna give it up.

116
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:11,017
Besides, we got these two gorgeous
girls tonight to keep us company.

117
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:14,218
Yeah, I almost wish that
morning didn't have to come.

118
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:18,037
That reminds me, what
happened to that broom boy?

119
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:20,117
I thought that for now we
should handle this without him.

120
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:22,517
I told him to go back
to town in the meantime.

121
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,430
What's this?

122
00:07:23,513 --> 00:07:25,122
A little fight with a boyfriend?

123
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,200
He's not my boyfriend.

124
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:29,150
Stop it.

125
00:07:29,233 --> 00:07:30,394
I don't even like him.

126
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:31,637
Let's go, Millie.

127
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:33,017
We have to go do the rounds now.

128
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:33,930
Coming!

129
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:35,490
Huh?

130
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:48,957
It sure is cold.

131
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:51,216
Hey, Meryl, is there something wrong?

132
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:52,597
It's nothing, really.

133
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,557
It's just that I know I've seen the
face in that picture somewhere before.

134
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:57,917
The only thing is, I
can't seem to place it.

135
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,977
Oh, you mean like a passing fancy?

136
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:01,360
A passing likeness.

137
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:04,465
I'm absolutely sure I've
seen that face before.

138
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,460
Who goes there?

139
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:10,420
Wait! Don't shoot!

140
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:14,420
Oh no, it's that man!

141
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:17,977
Well, what a pleasant surprise,
the two of you once again.

142
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:20,717
You can put your guns
away ladies. Obviously.

143
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,153
I've come here unarmed.

144
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,837
What the hell are you doing here?

145
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,197
I came to try and talk dad out of this.

146
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:28,280
Morgan means business this time!

147
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,400
Talk dad. Oh.

148
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:37,100
The picture.

149
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:40,100
Yep, that's me.

150
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:42,017
All right the unworthy son now.

151
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:42,930
Where is he?

152
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:49,981
What reason could you possibly have
to point a gun at your parents?

153
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:52,077
It's none of your business,

154
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:55,517
but if you must know, it's their own
fault for not listening to reason.

155
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:58,188
I had to do it or they'd
never get the hint.

156
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,240
You face!

157
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:02,290
Hey!

158
00:09:02,373 --> 00:09:03,203
What are you doing?

159
00:09:03,286 --> 00:09:05,220
Cut it out! Stop that! Millie!

160
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:11,960
You rotten ingrate, evil and stupid,
good-for-nothing awful son! What?

161
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,536
What's your problem?

162
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:15,805
What's all the commotion, huh?

163
00:09:16,060 --> 00:09:17,531
Who's fighting out there?

164
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:20,500
Oh, Badwick.

165
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:26,360
You mind telling me what in the
hell you think you're doing?

166
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:28,657
Look at you guys standing there.

167
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:30,577
You haven't taken care of a damn thing.

168
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:31,490
Uh, well,

169
00:09:31,573 --> 00:09:34,137
Badwick wanted just one more
chance to persuade his parents,

170
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:37,514
and we didn't really see any
harm in that, so we just...

171
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,020
He did, did he?

172
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:43,180
I hired him for his diligence,

173
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:46,057
but what's the point if he
can't even kill his own parents?

174
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:49,846
Evidently, I made an error in
judgment having any faith in him.

175
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,157
What do you think you're doing?

176
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,697
That's my car you just destroyed.

177
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:12,857
Oh well excuse me you probably
did something crooked to get it.

178
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:17,117
Anyway listen Mr Morgan
my father and little

179
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:19,257
brother's bail money is
riding on the success of

180
00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:21,377
this little scenario if
you try to take it out

181
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:24,077
of our pay you're gonna
get yourself flattened.

182
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:26,157
You're absolutely right
i can appreciate the

183
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:28,946
value of family i didn't
like that car anyhow.

184
00:10:30,020 --> 00:10:32,197
Great now that that's
settled we'll show you

185
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:34,986
the strength of our
steel-plated family bonds.

186
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:43,397
So you decided you're not going
to listen to me, no matter what?

187
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:45,245
We will not give him the deed.

188
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:48,857
Your little band of vigilantes isn't going
to be able to help you if you do this.

189
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:50,357
You'll all be slaughtered.

190
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:54,597
I think of Morgan as a child who wants a
priceless treasure he knows nothing about.

191
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:58,562
If not cared for properly, this
land would quickly dry up and die.

192
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:04,460
Badwick, my son, this
land lives and breathes.

193
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:08,619
You think land is more
important than your own life?

194
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:12,537
I don't understand how you
can so willingly continue

195
00:11:12,620 --> 00:11:16,000
to keep sacrificing everything
for this land. Damn you!

196
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:17,540
Max was right.

197
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:21,448
He chose to die instead of being
raised by worthless parents.

198
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:22,770
Huh?

199
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:41,860
The end.

200
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:47,850
Almost there!

201
00:11:47,933 --> 00:11:48,763
Ready?

202
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,070
Huh?

203
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:54,810
Huh?

204
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:57,250
Huh?

205
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:04,000
Ah?

206
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:07,620
Yeah, that was really smooth, Mom.

207
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:10,437
Now, place the next shot
about five yards over there.

208
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,717
Please don't hit the trees.

209
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:12,877
That wouldn't be right.

210
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,195
I see no point in it.

211
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:16,242
Jeez, you're ruining all my fun.

212
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,577
Wait, hold on a minute.

213
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:19,542
Do you have any idea who we are?

214
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:23,984
Patricia, Tonka-Tee, Jin-Pei, and
the one that I call Miss Kanta.

215
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:29,580
All together, we are the totally invincible
team of Marilyn, Nebraska and Friends.

216
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:36,630
What?

217
00:12:36,713 --> 00:12:38,377
You haven't done anything
so don't hog the limelight.

218
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:40,060
Oh, Mom, you're funny.

219
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:42,277
Don't be such a stick in the mud.

220
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:46,066
I sure hope that they're worth
all the money we're paying them.

221
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:47,752
All right, Mom, come on.

222
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:49,317
Now let's give Chin Pei a whirl.

223
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:50,341
What do you say?

224
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:54,600
Ready, take aim, and fire!

225
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,200
Hey! They're coming!

226
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,951
We gotta get out of here!

227
00:13:10,380 --> 00:13:11,297
What are they doing?

228
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:12,797
They're not supposed to be here yet!

229
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,821
What do they expect me to do now?

230
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:17,600
Come on, it's just about showtime!

231
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:20,360
Um, yeah, right, but...

232
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:23,020
It figures.

233
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:27,457
Anyone in the right mind
would just run from them.

234
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:28,658
That may be solved.

235
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:35,820
Mom? Dad?

236
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:37,557
Go ahead and run if you want.

237
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:40,960
I don't expect you to stay
here and die with us. What?

238
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:43,048
What are you talking about?

239
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,737
These guys are really serious.

240
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:49,397
And there's no telling
what they're gonna do.

241
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,310
No!

242
00:13:54,180 --> 00:13:55,500
Leave your minds!

243
00:13:57,380 --> 00:14:01,792
This whole thing has turned into a
real mess, what are we gonna do Meryl?

244
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:02,850
Meryl?

245
00:14:08,340 --> 00:14:10,620
Damn, we just can't stop him! Huh?

246
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:14,600
I'm sorry this happened.

247
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:17,017
You can leave now and
thanks for your help.

248
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,377
I'm so sorry!

249
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:20,080
Hey, it's all right.

250
00:14:30,220 --> 00:14:33,044
Well, have we come to an
understanding, old man?

251
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:34,830
Sure.

252
00:14:34,913 --> 00:14:37,897
I understand what a scoundrel
in a pig you really are.

253
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:40,420
Dad, stop that. Don't worry.

254
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:42,757
There's no way Morgan's
going to shoot him.

255
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:47,057
At least not yet, anyway, because the
land would never be his without the deed.

256
00:14:47,140 --> 00:14:49,400
I can't believe that crazy old man.

257
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,835
Why is he doing that?

258
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:55,716
Are you really that much of an idiot?

259
00:14:56,380 --> 00:14:59,180
He's doing it to save
the land, me, and you.

260
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:00,997
I can't believe you don't see that.

261
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:01,910
Huh?

262
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:05,597
I don't know how you've felt
about your father all these years,

263
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:09,562
but I'm sure he loves you and is
willing to risk his life for you.

264
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:15,377
I'm afraid it's a little late
for this lovey-dovey crap.

265
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:18,380
Unless we give in, Ma,
we're all gonna die here.

266
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:21,040
This land just eats money.

267
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:25,577
I'm not sure why it's so important to you,
but it's a burden I'm willing to take on.

268
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:27,000
Here is a new claim.

269
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:30,297
A way out of this mess that
is actually worth something.

270
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:32,157
I'll fill in the amount right now.

271
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:35,416
All you have to do is tell
me how many zeros you want.

272
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:38,337
I think my answer's pretty clear.

273
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:39,250
I'll beat it.

274
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:41,940
So you want an early death, do you?

275
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:43,290
Very well.

276
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:44,655
I'll accommodate you.

277
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:46,800
What should I do?

278
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:49,280
Go ahead and kill me.

279
00:15:49,540 --> 00:15:51,537
But the moment you do,
you lose everything.

280
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:54,326
Can't you see all the
witnesses standing here?

281
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:00,820
Did you say witnesses?

282
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:02,477
You've got to be kidding.

283
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:04,257
I won't leave a soul standing.

284
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:08,516
My job won't be finished here until
the last man is dead, I assure you.

285
00:16:10,660 --> 00:16:11,540
You can't!

286
00:16:15,460 --> 00:16:17,237
No, Millie! Excuse me,

287
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:18,897
but didn't your father
ever teach you that it's

288
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:21,237
wrong to take things that
belong to someone else?

289
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,732
Be careful, little lady!

290
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:26,122
Are you the tough little helper?

291
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:28,180
Yes, I am, now you be quiet!

292
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:29,690
Millie...

293
00:16:29,773 --> 00:16:31,157
You're wasting your time, little lady!

294
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:34,828
Doesn't matter, you're all
destined to become corpses anyway.

295
00:16:41,940 --> 00:16:42,770
Hmph!

296
00:16:42,853 --> 00:16:44,517
Charming as this is, I'm getting tired.

297
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:46,120
Let's get this over with.

298
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:47,257
I don't think so, Mr.

299
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,170
Morgan.

300
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:53,337
Now that I've heard your gruesome plan,
I'm afraid I can't let you off that easily.

301
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:54,717
Make even the slightest twitch,

302
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:57,417
and I'll be all over you and
your sick little band of thugs.

303
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,840
Oh, Meryl, I'm so glad you're here.

304
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:03,437
I would suggest that next time you
think a little bit more before you act,

305
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:05,097
Millie, you might live a lot longer.

306
00:17:05,180 --> 00:17:06,010
Right.

307
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:10,430
Badwick!

308
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,470
Badwick!

309
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:21,370
Freeze!

310
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:24,397
I just don't understand any of you.

311
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,857
Why did it have to come to this?

312
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:29,417
If you had only taken the money and sold
the land, we wouldn't have a problem.

313
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:32,077
No one would have to die and
we'd all be safe from harm.

314
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,020
I said freeze!

315
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:38,377
You know, Millie, when you got angry
before, you were right in confronting them.

316
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:40,097
We should be outraged when
someone threatens their

317
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:42,457
own parents and do whatever
we can to stop them.

318
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:44,011
It's extremely important.

319
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:45,430
Ha ha ha!

320
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:46,957
What the hell is that?

321
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:48,020
Are you serious?

322
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:52,808
Do you honestly believe that you can
turn the tide with those tiny terrangers?

323
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:56,197
Yeah, want to find out
what I can do with them?

324
00:17:56,280 --> 00:18:00,633
That is if you have the guts and want
to risk taking a chance on the odds.

325
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:02,810
Go on.

326
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:17,952
Alright, Morgan, enough!

327
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:19,620
I got the document!

328
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,457
I got what you've been asking for!

329
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:22,760
Son, don't do it!

330
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:25,060
Well done!

331
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:32,740
Get him now!

332
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:45,880
I can't! No!

333
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,440
I'll never make it!

334
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:50,980
But I have to try!

335
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:08,060
That was really amazing, Meryl!

336
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:10,120
I did that?

337
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:17,953
That makes us even now for
your help on the sand steamer.

338
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:20,802
Hey, is that all the time I get?

339
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:24,895
Well, then, what do you think of that?

340
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:26,697
Don't say she didn't warn you.

341
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:28,737
No one can escape the wrath
of Meryl's Derringers.

342
00:19:28,820 --> 00:19:30,997
Consider yourself fortunate
you're still alive.

343
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:34,977
Her next targets are going to be your
hearts and brains, and then you're through.

344
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,380
Are you insane?

345
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:38,617
That was nothing more than a lucky shot.

346
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:41,171
That gun couldn't possibly have done this.

347
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:43,199
Oh, could it have?

348
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:44,830
Nooo!

349
00:19:44,913 --> 00:19:45,959
How could this be?

350
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:49,747
Our Supergirl technique was
supposed to be totally invincible!

351
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:51,370
That's enough!

352
00:19:51,453 --> 00:19:52,283
Stop that!

353
00:19:52,366 --> 00:19:53,297
This hit, you blithering coward!

354
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:55,977
That advance payment I made you
wasn't cheap and I expect results!

355
00:19:56,060 --> 00:19:59,413
So get your act together right
now, do you understand me?

356
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:03,815
It's alright, Mother.

357
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:05,488
I'm sure cheap pay is fine.

358
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:07,192
Everything will be okay.

359
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:08,417
So go help him.

360
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:10,817
Or of course, if your son
means that much to you,

361
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,917
why don't you stop throwing him around?

362
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:13,830
Get off!

363
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:15,080
Get off!

364
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:16,937
I can't handle any more of this.

365
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:17,850
Let's beat it.

366
00:20:17,933 --> 00:20:18,763
Right.

367
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:23,694
What's wrong, my dear?

368
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:26,175
I think I might have pulled something.

369
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:28,685
It's gonna be all right, dear.

370
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:31,857
Yes, I'm sure it will, and
no matter what happens,

371
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:34,420
we have to understand it's what he wants.

372
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:36,346
We'll just have to trust him.

373
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:41,157
I don't know how to find the words to
thank you both for what you've done.

374
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:43,320
Especially you, Miss Merrill.

375
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:48,192
I want to share something with you from
an old man who raised an idiot son.

376
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:51,781
Everyone makes their own choices.

377
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:55,397
Nothing could compare to the love
between a parent and a child.

378
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:58,217
Your love for them doesn't
have to be a burden.

379
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:03,240
Instead of worrying about it, do
something more simple, yet very important.

380
00:21:03,780 --> 00:21:07,160
Walk your own path with
your head held high.

381
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:09,797
Your life is their life.

382
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:16,380
The fact that you are who you are helps
the people you love to live through you.

383
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:24,078
I don't know what is so
great about this stupid deed.

384
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:35,040
This is the real deed?

385
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:36,830
Yeah.

386
00:21:36,913 --> 00:21:37,840
Now it's in your hands.

387
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:40,497
Hey hold on a moment, sir?

388
00:21:40,580 --> 00:21:45,837
There seems to be one more claim transfer
in the envelope you need to look at it.

389
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:49,077
The beneficiary, as
written here, is Badwick.

390
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:50,600
Isn't that you?

391
00:21:59,900 --> 00:22:01,460
Yes, that's me.

392
00:22:04,780 --> 00:22:05,610
Yikes!

393
00:22:05,740 --> 00:22:08,040
Mira, we're never gonna make it!

394
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:09,800
I'm sorry, Millie.

395
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:13,697
This time it was actually my fault
for staying up all night riding.

396
00:22:13,780 --> 00:22:14,610
Mira.

397
00:22:18,060 --> 00:22:18,890
Mira.

398
00:22:21,020 --> 00:22:21,850
Daryl!

399
00:22:21,933 --> 00:22:22,763
What are you doing?

400
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:25,237
Dash's bus is getting ready to go!

401
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:26,757
They're gonna leave without us!

402
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:28,193
I'm coming, I'm coming!

403
00:23:31,220 --> 00:23:34,197
I'll see you

404
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:40,420
next time.

405
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:46,097
I'll see you in the

406
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:51,680
middle of the night

407
00:24:07,740 --> 00:24:09,500
People judge people.

408
00:24:09,780 --> 00:24:13,427
Lives are being cut short because
of someone's personal logic.

409
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:18,320
Mothers, fathers, friends, their entire
past instantly vanishes into thin air.

410
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:22,818
The question is, should this take
place at the whim of one individual?

411
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:27,141
A beautiful woman stood before the
corpses of the Roderick thieves.

412
00:24:27,520 --> 00:24:31,285
She told me that she was merely
discarding some useless garbage.

413
00:24:31,500 --> 00:24:36,000
Dominique the Cyclops told me to
just think of it as spring cleaning.
